Subject: arm64: dts: exynos7870-on7xelte: use in-band SDIO interrupts for Wi-Fi

The BCM43430 host-wake line (gpa2-2) reads low all the time on the
SM-G610F: the pin has the reset pull-down and the chip never releases it.
With the upstream "interrupts = <2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>" the out-of-band
interrupt fires about 18000 times per second; every time brcmfmac reads
an empty intstatus over SDIO (one dw-mci interrupt each), which keeps a
kworker about 40 % busy and adds ~35000 function-call IPIs per second.
Seen identically on 6.15 (PIO) and 7.3.4 (IDMAC). With
IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH the firmware does not come up (dongle not
responding, -110).

Drop the out-of-band interrupt so brcmfmac uses in-band SDIO interrupts
(mmc1 already has cap-sdio-irq). Measured on 7.3.4: mmc1 27
interrupts/s, total 9000/s instead of 70000/s, context switches
4700/s instead of 70000/s, Wi-Fi associated, 0 % ping loss.
Out-of-band wake is only needed for system suspend, which this phone
does not use.

Against: linux v7.3.4 + 0001-0013. License: GPL-2.0 (kernel DTS).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
@@ -883,9 +883,14 @@
 	wifi@1 {
 		compatible = "brcm,bcm43430a1-fmac", "brcm,bcm4329-fmac";
 		reg = <0x1>;
-		interrupt-names = "host-wake";
-		interrupt-parent = <&gpa2>;
-		interrupts = <2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		/*
+		 * No out-of-band host-wake interrupt: on this board gpa2-2 reads
+		 * low all the time (pull-down, line never released), so the
+		 * level-low OOB interrupt fired ~18000 times/s with an empty
+		 * intstatus and kept a core ~40 % busy; level-high stops the
+		 * firmware from coming up at all. In-band SDIO interrupts
+		 * (cap-sdio-irq on mmc1) work and fire only on real events.
+		 */
 
 		reset-gpios = <&gpd3 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	};
